                <pb facs="0346" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg252"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00 Elections/84: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grummon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-04T10:00:00-05:00">June 4, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>95. President Roy has announced in a press interview published in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nouvelliste</hi> that the reconstitution of the
                    legislative chambers will take place in October; that until that time the
                    Council of State will be maintained and that modifications in the present
                    electoral law will be made early in July.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grummon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
